From 6aaec4d7abb31aacb35dffa8eb136756f94c86d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:11:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(admin-tools): one settlement record per round; Risk
 Breaches, Battle Inspector, Price Audit and Risk Terminal read it

Settlement (directive, legacy Model A, tie) now writes a RoundValuation into
npc_round_audit.settlement after the financial transaction commits: real losing
and winning volume net of hedges, commission and its source, net real loser pool,
real winners' profit, house cash result (real money in minus out), shortfall
(paid beyond the net real pool), simulator figures, user counts, refunds.

Risk Breaches: valuation-driven breach / house-cash / real-winner scopes, period
summary over the whole window, resolution on every row, exact-instant custom
ranges, detail with per-user cash PnL from the ledger, breach alert scanner.
Battle Inspector: settlement panel from the record, real money net of hedges by
the round's model, RPC stakes separated, organic-aware live winner, participants
per user per side, CANCELLED branch, start_at/end_at.
Price Movement Audit: one flag rule (expected-vs-actual variance; swing fallback
flagged as such), expected path = formula for real trades + recorded NPC moves,
freeze seconds and config source stored atomically with the snapshot, price ticks
stamped with the engine event time, validated status, honest CSV, truncation flag.
Risk Terminal: engine tick projects with the settling model (directive for organic
rounds), company_net_position is the house cash result with shortfall, Redis
buffers read for live rounds, in-flight guard, last tick served by REST, alerts
endpoint, dead injection code removed.
Also: settlement folds the recorded price path into roundHigh/roundLow and writes
it back; duplicate stake ledger rows from the async writer deduplicated per batch.

Specs: round-valuation, directive-scenarios, round-context, price-audit-replay-hybrid;
risk-terminal regression harness covers legacy and organic projections.

